From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:30:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] setup: scope LLVM targets to build on riscv64 linux

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; mirrors the existing macOS arm64 branch below it]

my_cmake_build.run() never passes -DLLVM_TARGETS_TO_BUILD on Linux (only
macOS arm64 and Windows get an explicit value); src/interpreter/
CMakeLists.txt does have a `ROOT_ARCHITECTURE MATCHES riscv64` branch that
would set it to "RISCV;NVPTX", the same shape as its AArch64/ARM/PowerPC/
SystemZ branches, but ROOT_ARCHITECTURE is never set in this cling-only
build (src/CMakeLists.txt never include()s ROOT's SetUpLinux.cmake), so
that branch is unreachable and dispatch falls through to the "all" case:
every LLVM backend (x86, arm, aarch64, powerpc, systemz, riscv, ...), not
just the one the build runs on. That turns an already multi-hour
from-source LLVM+Clang+Cling build into one compiling backends that can
never be used on this host.

LLVM_TARGETS_TO_BUILD is a CACHE variable; src/interpreter/CMakeLists.txt
only set()s it (no FORCE), so a value supplied on the cmake command line
-- as this patch adds -- wins over that fallback, the same way the macOS
arm64 branch immediately above already overrides it for that platform.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 cling/setup.py | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cling/setup.py b/cling/setup.py
index 8dbdf4e..d390f5b 100755
--- a/cling/setup.py
+++ b/cling/setup.py
@@ -169,6 +169,10 @@ class my_cmake_build(_build):
             import platform
             if 'arm64' in platform.machine():
                 CMAKE_COMMAND += ['-DLLVM_TARGETS_TO_BUILD=ARM;AArch64;NVPTX']
+        elif 'linux' in sys.platform:
+            import platform
+            if 'riscv64' in platform.machine():
+                CMAKE_COMMAND += ['-DLLVM_TARGETS_TO_BUILD=RISCV;NVPTX']
         CMAKE_COMMAND.append('-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX='+prefix)
 
         log.info('Running cmake for cppyy-cling: %s', ' '.join(CMAKE_COMMAND))
